From: Kissshot <ttyinzg@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 13:24:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat(session): let a log-only append declare itself
 ignorable
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The ignorable envelope field decides whether a reader that does not
recognize an event type may skip it or must refuse the whole log. Seed
validation, both persistence backends, and the wire schema already
honored it, but no writer could set one: append's only optional
parameter was SurfaceIntent, and the envelope was built without the
field, so every event type outside this build's vocabulary was
required-on-read. This supplies the missing producer the session-log
version mechanism reserved for its first user.

The options parameter now selects one of two disjoint types by event
class: a SurfaceEventType keeps requiring SurfaceIntent, and every other
type accepts an optional LogIntent carrying ignorable. Disjoint types
rather than one merged object make two mistakes unrepresentable — a
surface placement on a log-only event, and an ignorable marker on a
message-producing one. The second matters most: a surface event is
always a recognized model-visible type, so a reader skipping one would
silently drop model context.

SESSION_FORMAT_VERSION stays 0; the field was already in the envelope.
