 Only `assistant/message` may carry a present empty `sourceEventSeqs`; when the field is absent, the event does not record which earlier events produced the message, and the provider may still have emitted chunks.
 
+### `LogIntent` — the log-only counterpart
+
+```ts type-equiv
+/**
+ * Reader-compatibility declaration for a log-only event in {@link Session.append}.
+ * Optional on log-only events and unavailable on message-producing ones: a
+ * {@link SurfaceEventType} is always recognized by any reader and is
+ * model-visible, so skipping one could never be safe.
+ */
+interface LogIntent {
+  /**
+   * Set `true` only on a purely informational record whose loss cannot affect
+   * reconstruction, marking it skippable by a reader that does not recognize
+   * its type. Omission means required, which is the safe default: see
+   * {@link SessionEvent.ignorable} for the full envelope contract.
+   */
+  ignorable?: true
+}
+```
+
+The two option types are disjoint by event class, so the compiler admits neither a surface placement on a log-only event nor an `ignorable` marker on a message-producing one. Omission keeps an event required on read, and a reader meeting an unrecognized required type refuses the log rather than reconstructing a session missing an event that may change how the rest is interpreted.
+
 ### `SessionSurface` — the live readonly surface projection
 
 `Session.surface` returns the session's stable `SessionSurface` view. The same incremental manager validates append candidates before commit and advances this projection from committed events; callers can observe membership and replacement generation but cannot invoke validation.
